ase URLs with a non-lowercase `password` query parameter name.\\n<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->\\n\\n<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 8da3b6d0-a861-4d3e-bcd1-4d0151a9a163 -->\\n\\n<!-- LOCATIONS START\\nredact/redact.go#L273-L280\\nLOCATIONS END -->\\n<div><a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix in Web\\\" width=\\\"99\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"></picture></a></div>\\n\\n\\n<sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 83085ef5ca3aa3508d5f5aa047bd4098cfca388f. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"cursor[bot]\", \"name\": \"cursor[bot]\", \"email\": null, \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4\", \"id\": 206951365}, \"id\": 3148254385, \"pull_request_review_id\": 4181997750, \"in_reply_to_id\": null, \"created_at\": \"2026-04-27T15:03:06Z\", \"review\": null, \"side\": \"RIGHT\", \"line\": 308, \"start_line\": null, \"path\": \"redact/redact.go\", \"body_html\": \"<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Database URL password check is case-sensitive unlike other detectors</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Medium Severity</strong></p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">hasDatabaseURLSecret</code> uses <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">u.Query().Get(\\\"password\\\")</code> which is case-sensitive, while the <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">databaseURLPattern</code> regex that feeds it is case-insensitive (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">(?i)</code>). A database URL like <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">postgresql://host/db?user=svc&amp;Password=secret</code> would be matched by the pattern but <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Get(\\\"password\\\")</code> returns empty for the key <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Password</code>. The three sibling detectors (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">hasJDBCPassword</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">hasKeywordDSNPassword</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">hasSemicolonConnectionPassword</code>) all delegate to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">hasNonPlaceholderPasswordAssignment</code> which uses the case-insensitive <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">passwordAssignmentRegex</code>, so they handle <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Password</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">PASSWORD</code>, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">pwd</code> variants correctly. This inconsistency creates a credential-leak gap specific to non-JDBC database URLs with a non-lowercase <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">password</code> query parameter name.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div dir=\\\"auto\\\"><a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\"><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\\\"true\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/ad0023cf5d57d12b64eac5658cacf0b8767b5355ef9049b11b793fe92040ac79/68747470733a2f2f637572736f722e636f6d2f6173736574732f696d616765732f6669782d696e2d637572736f722d6461726b2e706e67\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https