wer[bot]","name":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4","id":175728472},"id":4181136702,"pull_request_review_id":null,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-04-27T13:08:23Z","review":"COMMENTED","side":null,"line":null,"start_line":null,"path":null,"body_html":"<h2 dir=\"auto\">Pull request overview</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR strengthens Entire CLI’s automatic transcript redaction by adding more secret detectors (beyond entropy + gitleaks) and expanding regression coverage to reduce both under- and over-redaction in common credential formats.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Changes:</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add redaction for full private key blocks, credentialed URIs, database DSNs/URLs, and bounded password-like key/value pairs.</li>\n<li>Enhance JSON/JSONL redaction to support key-scoped replacements for structured credential fields.</li>\n<li>Expand unit tests and update security/privacy documentation to reflect the new detection layers.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Reviewed changes</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Copilot reviewed 3 out of 3 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\"table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>File</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>redact/redact.go</td>\n<td>Adds new secret detectors (private keys, credentialed URIs, connection strings, bounded credentials) and extends JSONL replacement handling.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>redact/redact_test.go</td>\n<td>Adds extensive coverage for new redaction behaviors, including guardrails against over-redaction.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>docs/security-and-privacy.md</td>\n<td>Updates documentation to describe the expanded automatic secret redaction methods.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>"},{"url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1045#issuecomment-4327976929","body":"@bugbot review","user":{"login":"peyton-alt","name":"peyton-alt","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4","id":249787869},"id":4327976929,"pull_request_review_id":null,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-04-27T14:53:23Z","review":null,"side":null,"line":null,"start_line":null,"path":null,"body_html":"<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/BugBot/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/BugBot\">@BugBot</a> review</p>"},{"url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1045#discussion_r3148254385","body":"### Database URL password check is case-sensitive unlike other detectors\n\n**Medium Severity**\n\n<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->\n`hasDatabaseURLSecret` uses `u.Query().Get(\"password\")` which is case-sensitive, while the `databaseURLPattern` regex that feeds it is case-insensitive (`(?i)`). A database URL like `REDACTED` would be matched by the pattern but `Get(\"password\")` returns empty for the key `Password`. The three sibling detectors (`hasJDBCPassword`, `hasKeywordDSNPassword`, `hasSemicolonConnectionPassword`) all delegate to `hasNonPlaceholderPasswordAssignment` which uses the case-insensitive `passwordAssignmentRegex`, so they handle `Password`, `PASSWORD`, and `pwd` variants correctly. This inconsistency creates a credential-leak gap specific to non-JDBC database URLs with a non-lowercase `password` query parameter name.\n<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->\n\n<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 8da3b6d0-a861-4d3e-bcd1-4d0151a9a163 -->\n\n<!-- LOCATIONS START\nredact/redact.go#L273-L280\nLOCATIONS END -->\n<div><a href=\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\"><img alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" width=\"115\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\"><img alt=\"Fix in Web\" width=\"99\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a></div>\n\n\n<sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 83085ef5ca3aa3508d5f5aa047bd4098cfca388f. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n","user":{"login":"cursor[bot]","name":"cursor[bot]","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","id":206951365},"id":3148254385,"pull_request_review_id":4181997750,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-04-27T15:03:06Z","review":null,"side":"RIGHT","line":308,"start_line":null,"path":"redact/redact.go","body_html":"<h3 dir=\"auto\">Database URL password check is case-sensitive unlike other detectors</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Medium Severity</strong></p>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">hasDatabaseURLSecret</code> uses <code class=\"notranslate\">u.Query().Get(\"password\")</code> which is case-sensitive, while the <code class=\"notranslate\">databaseURLPattern</code> regex that feeds it is case-insensitive (<code class=\"notranslate\">(?i)</code>). A database URL like <code class=\"notranslate\">postgresql://host/db?user=svc&amp;Password=secret</code> would be matched by the pattern but <code class=\"notranslate\">Get(\"password\")</code> returns empty for the key <code class=\"notranslate\">Password</code>. The three sibling detectors (<code class=\"notranslate\">hasJDBCPassword</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">hasKeywordDSNPassword</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">hasSemicolonConnectionPassword</code>) all delegate to <code class=\"notranslate\">hasNonPlaceholderPasswordAssignment</code> which uses the case-insensitive <code class=\"notranslate\">passwordAssignmentRegex</code>, so they handle <code class=\"notranslate\">Password</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">PASSWORD</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">pwd</code> variants correctly. This inconsistency creates a credential-leak gap specific to non-JDBC database URLs with a non-lowercase <code class=\"notranslate\">password</code> query parameter name.</p>\n\n\n\n<div dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" rel=\"nofollow\"><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/ad0023cf5d57d12b64eac5658cacf0b8767b5355ef9049b11b793fe92040ac79/68747470733a2f2f637572736f722e636f6d2f6173736574732f696d616765732f6669782d696e2d637572736f722d6461726b2e706e67\" data-canonical-src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/ab92f9c38cf0cf573911a22e2a83b5c9741bd339d7e103a684304a2626d54846/68747470733a2f2f637572736f722e636f6d2f6173736574732f696d616765732f6669782d696e2d637572736f722d6c696768742e706e67\" data-canonical-src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\"><img alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" width=\"115\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/ad0023cf5d57d12b64eac5658cacf0b8767b5355ef9049b11b793fe92040ac79/68747470733a2f2f637572736f722e636f6d2f6173736574732f696d616765732f6669782d696e2d637572736f722d6461726b2e706e67\" data-canonical-src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></themed-picture></a> <a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\" rel=\"nofollow\"><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"h