{"timestamp":"2026-05-13T14:47:28.019Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Because it parsed each JSONL line correctly, but then scanned each decoded string value in isolation.\n\nFor the working case, the decoded value is one string containing the whole key:\n\n```text\nkey:\nREDACTED\"}\n{\"content\":\"payload-line-1\"}\n{\"content\":\"payload-line-2\"}\n{\"content\":\"-----END OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----\"}\n```\n\n`JSONLContent` unmarshals line 1, calls `String(\"-----BEGIN OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----\")`, then line 2, calls `String(\"payload-line-1\")`, etc. Betterleaks’ private-key rule needs enough surrounding content to match a full private-key block, so no individual string had the whole pattern.\n\nEntropy also did not reliably save us because the OpenSSH payload line can be long but structurally base64-ish, and depending on the exact line it may not cross the current entropy rule in the way we need. The begin/end markers are also low entropy, so entropy will not catch them.\n\nThe fix I added makes Entire not depend on seeing the full block: it redacts private-key begin/end markers and OpenSSH key payload fragments too.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
